 "text": "Recorder's Office / Newton County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nNewton County\nThe Official Government Website for Newton County, Indiana\nDocuments | Site Tools\nSearch\nSearch Submit\nStart Content\nToggle Menu\nHome\nAbout Community Events\nCounty Demographics\nDocument Center\nEmployment Opportunities\nEvents Calendar\nResident Information\nCourthouse Assessor\nAuditor\nClerk\nCourts\nProbation\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nTreasurer\nCourthouse Directory\nGovernment Center Adult Education\nBuilding Department\nCoroner's Office\nCounty Commissioners Commissioners Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Commissioners\nCounty Council Council Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Council Members\nHealth Department\nPark Board\nPurdue Extension\nRecycling\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nVeteran's Service Officer\nWIC\nWorkOne\nCounty Facilities Ambulance Service\nAnimal Control\nCommunications Center\nDepartment Child Services\nDivision of Family Resources\nEmergency Management Agency\nHighway Department\nMaintenace Department\nMap of County Offices\nSearch Locations by Name\nSurveyor's Office\nSheriff Dept In Remembrance\nNewton County Jail\nContact Ask a Question\nBoards & Commissions Board of Zoning Appeals\nDrainage Board\nPlan Commission\nPlat Commission\nCounty Departments A-G Ambulance Services\nAnimal Control\nAssessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nBuilding Department\nClerk of Courts\nCoroner's Office\nEconomic Development\nElections & Voting\nEmergency Management Agency\nEmergency Medical Services\nGIS Services\nCounty Departments H-Z Health Department\nHighway Department\nMaintenance Department\nNewton County Extension Office\nProbation Department\nProsecutor's Office\nRecorder's Office\nRecycling\nSheriff's Department\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSurveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nZoning\nVeteran's Service Officer\nSubmit an Online Form\nView the County Staff Directory\nEmployee Resources Doculivery\nEmployee Webmail\nEmployment Application\nYou are here: Home » Officials » Recorder's Office\nRecorder's Office\nThe elective office of county recorder was the first local office created by the Constitution of the state of Indiana in 1816. It is the primary duty of county recorders to record instruments submitted for recording and maintaining those records for perpetuity. Documents for statistical record keeping purposes fall into five categories: (1) deeds and other conveyances, (2) mortgages and other liens and their releases, (3) miscellaneous documents, (4) plats, surveys and floor plans, (5) uniform commercial code documents.\nYour County Recorder:\nRecords any instrument submitted for recording, providing it meets essential requirements.\nRecords Deeds, Mortgages, Assignments, Releases, Powers of Attorney, Real Estate Contracts, Annexations, Trustee Elections, Affidavits, Final Decrees, Surveys, Federal Tax Liens, Mechanics Liens, Military Discharges, Articles of Incorporation, Cemetery Deeds, Bonds, Plats, Condominiums, Firms Doing Business Under Assumed Names, Delinquent Sewer Liens, and Miscellaneous Instruments.\nFiles Uniform Commercial Code instruments.\nSupplies copies of any instrument and certifies to those recorded upon request. (Fee charged)\nPermit Bonds are no longer required to be recorded. Permit Bonds are still a county requirement; however, they are to be submitted to the Building Department ONLY .\nUseful Links\nUseful Links\ndoxpop.com | | |\nContact Us\nRecorder's Office\n201 N 3rd St\nKentland, IN 47951\nGet Directions\n|\nLocation/Facility Details\nPhone: (888) 663-9866 x 1401\nFax: (219) 474-9245\nEmail Us\nStaff Directory\nOffice Hours:\nMonday-Friday 8:00 a.m.-4:00 p.m.\nTopics of Interest\nDocuments Available Online\nFee Schedule\nMore Information\nDocument Center News\nUseful Links\nForms & Applications\nSite Design and Content Copyright © 2026 Newton County, IN\nSite Design and Content Management by\nCORE Business Technologies\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use",
